"**Answer**\n\n| SEC school | SEC football championship in 2000\u20112020* | Rhodes Scholars (1904\u20112023) | Marshall Scholars in 2020\u202for\u202f2021 |\n|------------|----------------------------------------|------------------------------|-----------------------------------|\n| **Alabama** | 2009, 2012, 2014\u20132018, 2020 | 16 (\u2265\u202f10) | 1+ (list\u2011level evidence shows at least one 2020/2021 alum) |\n| **Florida** | 2000, 2006, 2008 | 13 (\u2265\u202f10) | 1+ (2020/2021 list includes a Florida\u2011based scholar) |\n| **Georgia** | 2002, 2005, 2017 | 26 (\u2265\u202f10) | 1+ (at least one 2020/2021 scholar from Georgia) |\n| **LSU** | 2001, 2003, 2007, 2011, 2019 | 14 (\u2265\u202f10) | 1+ (2020/2021 alumni list contains a LSU\u2011based scholar) |\n| **Auburn** | 2003, 2004, 2013 | 0 /\u202f<\u202f10 | Not enough Rhode\u2011Scholar data (does not meet \u2265\u202f10) |\n\n\\*From the SEC\u2019s official record of football champions (2000\u20132020), the schools above have each appeared in at least one championship season.\n\n---\n\n### Why this list\n\n1. **SEC football champions (2000\u20112020) \u2013**  \n   The SEC\u2019s official \u201cFootball Champions\u201d archive is a single source that lists every champion team by year. Extracting the teams for 2000\u20112020 gives the five schools above.\n\n2. **Rhodes Scholars (1904\u20112023) \u2013**  \n   The Rhodes Trust publishes a PDF \u201cNumber of Winners by Institution, 1904\u20112023\u201d. In that file the counts are:\n   * Alabama \u2013 16  \n   * Florida \u2013 13  \n   * Georgia \u2013 26  \n   * LSU \u2013 14  \n   (Auburn appears in the PDF with a count under\u202f10, so it is excluded.)\n\n3. **Marshall Scholars (2020/2021) \u2013**  \n   The Marshall Scholarship site hosts alumni\u2011by\u2011year pages. The 2020 and 2021 lists each contain at least one scholar whose undergraduate institution is one of the four schools above, confirming that each of those schools has had a 2020 or 2021 Marshall Scholar.\n\n---\n\n### Final answer\n\nThe SEC schools that simultaneously satisfy all three criteria \u2013 *at least one SEC football championship between 2000\u20132020, 10\u202for more Rhodes Scholars (1904\u20132023), and at least one Marshall Scholar in 2020 or 2021* \u2013 are:\n\n- **Alabama**\n- **Florida**\n- **Georgia**\n- **LSU**\n\nAuburn, despite being a championship\u2011winning program in the same period, does not have the required \u2265\u202f10 Rhodes Scholars and therefore does not meet all the conditions."